This procedure is equivalent to interpolation with Taylor's formula 3.6.4.

**Example 18**.: _In the plane triangle \(ABC\), \(a\)=\(123\), \(B\)=\(29^{\circ}16^{\prime}\), \(c\)=\(321\); find \(A\), \(b\)._

\(b^{2}\)=\(a^{2}\)+\(c^{2}\)-\(2ac\)\(\cos\)\(B\)=\((123)^{2}\)+\((321)^{2}\)

\(-2\)\((123)\)\((321)\)\(\cos\)\(29^{\circ}16^{\prime}\)

\(b\)=\(221.99934\)\(00\)

\(\sin\)\(A\)=\(\dfrac{a\sin\,B}{b}\)=\(\dfrac{(123)(4.48887\,50196)}{221.99934\,00}\)

\(A\)=\(15^{9}42^{\prime}56.469^{\prime\prime}\).

